      "content": "That's exactly the kind of non-answer I was talking about. You're just hedging. But look, even if you won't pick a person, you can at least address the logic. The whole idea of using government spending to \"stimulate\" an economy that is already dealing with massive inflation just sounds like you're pouring gasoline on a fire. It seems pretty scientifically obvious that more spending drives prices up further. Are you saying there's actually a legitimate economic argument for Miller's plan to lower inflation, or is that just a fantasy?",
